  ---
  The Core Opportunity

  Your ecommerce app has real data (products, users, orders, balances) — that's the perfect grounding for an agent. Instead of a
  generic chatbot, you can build one that reasons over live data and takes real actions.

  ---
  Feature Ideas (grouped by complexity)

  Tier 1 — Product Intelligence (showcases RAG)

  - Semantic product search — "I need something for video calls" → embedds query, finds Webcam via vector similarity over product
  descriptions
  - Use-case matching — "I'm setting up a home office" → agent recommends a bundle (monitor stand + keyboard + webcam)
  - Budget-aware suggestions — "What can I get for under $100?" → filters live product data
  - Product comparison — "Compare the laptop vs the keyboard" → structured side-by-side with pros/cons

  Tier 2 — Shopping Actions (showcases Tool Use / Agentic)

  - Add to cart via chat — "Add 2 webcams to my cart" → agent calls a tool that updates the cart context
  - Cart awareness — "What's in my cart?" / "Can I afford what's in my cart?"
  - Balance check — "What's the most expensive thing I can buy right now?"

  Tier 3 — Order & Support (showcases Multi-step Reasoning)

  - Order lookup — "What did I last order?" → agent fetches order history
  - Refund processing — "I want a refund on my last order" → agent checks eligibility, confirms with user, calls refund API
  - Refund policy reasoning — agent applies rules (e.g. "only within 30 days") before allowing refund

  Tier 4 — Advanced Patterns (showcases Multi-Agent / Memory)

  - Router agent → delegates to specialist sub-agents: ShoppingAgent, SupportAgent
  - Conversation memory — remembers "I told you I have a $200 budget" across turns
  - ReAct loop visible in UI — show the agent's Thought → Action → Observation chain (great for demo!)

  ---
  What Skills/Tools the Agent Would Have

  search_products(query, max_price?)   ← RAG over product catalog
  get_product(product_id)              ← live DB lookup
  compare_products(id_a, id_b)         ← structured comparison
  get_order_history(user_id)           ← live DB lookup
  submit_refund(order_id)              ← mutates DB
  get_cart()                           ← reads cart state
  add_to_cart(product_id, qty)         ← mutates cart state
  get_user_balance(user_id)            ← live DB lookup

  ---
  Key Architecture Decision

  The agent lives in the backend (Python/LangChain), and the frontend just has a chat UI that streams responses. The agent has
  access to your existing FastAPI DB session — so it can read/write real data.




